      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">107</data>
      <data key="d13">259</data>
      <data key="d14">class _LockedAppender:</data>
      <data key="d15">Append-only writer that survives several processes sharing one file.

    Locking is advisory and per-write: the lock is taken, one whole line is
    written and flushed, and the lock is released. Two servers configured with
    the same `--audit-log` therefore interleave whole records rather than
    shredding each other's lines.

    A sink that cannot be opened at all leaves `_fh` None and every method a
    no-op. The constructor holds the same line `write` does: an audit file the
    operator mistyped is a degraded log, not a server that refuses to start,
    and the stderr copy of every </data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="4076.10" y="689.15" width="142.18" height="30.55" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_LockedAppender</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
