      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/bugreport.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">210</data>
      <data key="d13">270</data>
      <data key="d14">def _edge_quality(out: Path) -&gt; dict[str, Any]:</data>
      <data key="d15">How much of the graph is confident, and how it was extracted.

    This is the single most useful block for an "incorrect relationship"
    report: it says whether the repository as a whole resolves cleanly or is
    dominated by ambiguous name matches, which changes what the reported edge
    means. Counts only -- no ids, no paths.</data>
