    <node id="sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::_is_repo2graph_manifest">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::_is_repo2graph_manifest</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_is_repo2graph_manifest</data>
      <data key="d10">_is_repo2graph_manifest</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/doctor.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">350</data>
      <data key="d13">367</data>
      <data key="d14">def _is_repo2graph_manifest(manifest_file: Path) -&gt; bool:</data>
      <data key="d15">True only if `manifest_file` parses as a repo2graph manifest.json.

    A bare `agent/` directory or a `chunks.jsonl` are not proof of a
    repo2graph index -- both names collide with unrelated projects (agent
    frameworks, ML repos with their own chunk files). The manifest's
    "format" key, written by export.write_manifest as "repo2graph/1", is
    the only reliable signal. A missing or unparseable manifest means "not
    our index", not "corrupt index" -- check_artifact_integrity only
    reports corruption once this function has confirmed the directory is
    actually ours.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1414.92" y="1038.00" width="160.32" height="34.45" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_is_repo2graph…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::_find_index_dir">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::_find_index_dir</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_find_index_dir</data>
      <data key="d10">_find_index_dir</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/doctor.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">370</data>
      <data key="d13">401</data>
      <data key="d14">def _find_index_dir(path: Path) -&gt; Path | None:</data>
      <data key="d15">Locate an existing repo2graph index directory if present.

    ".r2g" is repo2graph's own default -o name (cli.py) and collides with
    nothing else, so a bare agent/ or chunks.jsonl found there is already
    corroborating evidence -- including a corrupt manifest.json, which
    check_artifact_integrity should go on to report as broken. Anywhere
    else, "agent/" and "chunks.jsonl" are generic names that unrelated
    projects (agent frameworks, ML repos) use too, so only a manifest.json
    that actually parses as ours counts as proof.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1599.25" y="1038.00" width="151.25" height="32.50" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_find_index_dir</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
