    <node id="sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::counts_as_call">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::counts_as_call</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">counts_as_call</data>
      <data key="d10">counts_as_call</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/edgemeta.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">83</data>
      <data key="d13">98</data>
      <data key="d14">def counts_as_call(e: dict[str, Any]) -&gt; bool:</data>
      <data key="d15">Whether a CALLS edge makes its target "called" for rankings/entrypoints.

    Gated on what the edge is, not only its number: an untyped-receiver
    builtin (`d.get()` -&gt; `_AppCtxGlobals.get`) never counts; a scoped
    fan-out (overloads, same class/file, through an import) always does; a
    global-name or same-module guess counts only at or above
    OVERVIEW_MIN_CALL_CONFIDENCE. An edge without `resolution_kind` (an older
    index) falls back to the threshold alone.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6373.03" y="1038.00" width="142.50" height="32.50" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">counts_as_call</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::tree_sitter_method">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::tree_sitter_method</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">tree_sitter_method</data>
      <data key="d10">tree_sitter_method</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
