      <data key="d13">124</data>
      <data key="d14">def tree_sitter_method(lang: str | None) -&gt; str:</data>
      <data key="d15">`tree-sitter/python`, or plain `tree-sitter` when the language is unknown.

    The language is part of the method on purpose: the same edge type carries
    different weight from different grammars, and a consumer that has learned
    to distrust, say, the C fallback needs to be able to say so.</data>
