    <node id="sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::evidence">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/edgemeta.py::evidence</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">evidence</data>
      <data key="d10">evidence</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/edgemeta.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">127</data>
      <data key="d13">138</data>
      <data key="d14">def evidence(path: str | None, line: int | None) -&gt; dict[str, Any] | None:</data>
      <data key="d15">An `{"path", "line"}` record, or None when there is no line to point at.

    None is a real answer, not a gap to paper over: a CONTAINS edge between a
    directory and a file is not written down anywhere, so claiming a line for
    it would be a fabricated citation — the exact failure this module exists
    to prevent. Line numbers are 1-based, matching every editor and every
    `path:line` convention.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6690.58" y="1038.00" width="86.40" height="31.20" />
