    <node id="sym:repo2graph/export.py::atomic_write">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/export.py::atomic_write</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">atomic_write</data>
      <data key="d10">atomic_write</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/export.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">52</data>
      <data key="d13">71</data>
      <data key="d14">def atomic_write(path: Path, mode: str = "w", **open_kw: Any) -&gt; Iterator[IO[Any]]:</data>
      <data key="d15">Write via a sibling temp file renamed onto `path` only on a clean exit.

    A crash, exception or Ctrl-C mid-write then leaves the previous artifact (or
    none) intact rather than a truncated file that `query`/`map` would choke on.
    The temp file is in the target's own directory, so os.replace is atomic.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6107.70" y="1114.00" width="182.50" height="47.45" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
