    <node id="sym:repo2graph/export.py::write_jsonl">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/export.py::write_jsonl</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">write_jsonl</data>
      <data key="d10">write_jsonl</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/export.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">137</data>
      <data key="d13">154</data>
      <data key="d14">def write_jsonl(path: Path, rows: Iterable[Any]) -&gt; int:</data>
      <data key="d15">Stream `rows` to `path` as JSONL; return how many were written.

    newline="\n" (ISS-28) + atomic: a crash mid-write must not leave a truncated
    last line that read_jsonl's json.loads then dies on. Streaming means `rows`
    may be a generator (build_chunks) that is never fully materialised.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="7117.43" y="1114.00" width="111.60" height="31.20" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
