      <data key="d10">parse_all</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/graph.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1238</data>
      <data key="d13">1273</data>
      <data key="d14">def parse_all(files, jobs: int, config=None):</data>
      <data key="d15">Read and parse every file, in discovery order, across `jobs` processes.

    tree-sitter parsing is CPU bound and dominates a large build, so this is
    the difference between one core and all of them. Order is preserved, which
    keeps node ids and edge order identical to a serial run.

    Every worker runs `silence_worker_io` first, so the pool is safe to start
    from a process whose stdin/stdout are a protocol stream rather than a
    terminal -- which is what `repo2graph-mcp`'s auto-build is (#90).</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3538.95" y="1292.00" width="112.58" height="37.05" />
