      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">908</data>
      <data key="d13">917</data>
      <data key="d14">def _receiver_kind(src: bytes, node) -&gt; str:</data>
      <data key="d15">Classify what a call is made on: "none", "self" or "other".

    "none" is a bare call (`helper()`), "self" is a call on the calling object
    (`self.x()`, `this.x()`, `super().x()`), and "other" is a call on anything
    else (`d.get()`, `os.environ.get()`, `self.cache.get()`). `_callee_name`
    drops the receiver, so without this `graph.build` cannot tell
    `self.get()` from `some_dict.get()`.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
