      <data key="d14">def _json_secret_value_ok(value: str) -&gt; bool:</data>
      <data key="d15">True if a JSON value under a secret-ish key looks like a real credential.

    Requires a letter *and* a digit, or three of the four character classes
    (lower, upper, digit, symbol). That keeps `"password": "Passwort"` (an i18n
    label) and `"tokenType": "access-token"` indexable while every generated
    password or key -- and every human one with a digit in it -- is caught.</data>
