    <node id="sym:repo2graph/status.py::compute_freshness">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/status.py::compute_freshness</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">compute_freshness</data>
      <data key="d10">compute_freshness</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/status.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">169</data>
      <data key="d13">327</data>
      <data key="d14">def compute_freshness(repo: Path, idx_dir: Path, agent_dir: Path) -&gt; Freshness:</data>
      <data key="d15">Three independent signals that the index no longer matches the tree.

    Cheapest first, and each one degrades to a note rather than an error:

    1. The commit recorded in `manifest.json` against the tree's `HEAD`. One
       subprocess, exact for committed state, silent on a non-git tree.
    2. The file set discovery finds now against the one `index.state.json`
       recorded -- a set difference over paths, no file reads.
    3. A real sha256 for each file whose mtime is newer than `manifest.json`.
       The mtime *only chooses what to hash*: a file touched but not changed
       hashes</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="4723.10" y="1891.60" width="269.23" height="57.85" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">compute_freshn…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
