    <node id="sym:scripts/make_demo_gif.py::build_frames">
      <data key="d0">sym:scripts/make_demo_gif.py::build_frames</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">build_frames</data>
      <data key="d10">build_frames</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">scripts/make_demo_gif.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">180</data>
      <data key="d13">205</data>
      <data key="d14">def build_frames(scenes):</data>
      <data key="d15">scenes: list of (command, output_lines[, prompt]). Returns frames.

    The prompt is per scene because not every scene is a shell: an MCP tool
    call is not something anyone types at a `$`, and drawing it as one would
    teach the reader the wrong thing about how the server is driven.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1135.40" y="2134.55" width="117.50" height="30.55" />
