      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">118</data>
      <data key="d13">134</data>
      <data key="d14">def jwks_with(**over):</data>
      <data key="d15">A one-key JWKS built from the test key, with fields overridden or dropped.

    `_ABSENT` as a value removes the field outright, which is how a JWK that
    never declares `n`, `e`, `use` or `key_ops` gets expressed. `jwks_doc()`
    above is the same document; this one exists so a test can name the single
    field it is interested in and leave every other one correct.</data>
