    <node id="sym:tests/test_auth.py::test_an_expired_ttl_refetches">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_auth.py::test_an_expired_ttl_refetches</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_an_expired_ttl_refetches</data>
      <data key="d10">test_an_expired_ttl_refetches</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_auth.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">561</data>
      <data key="d13">582</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_an_expired_ttl_refetches():</data>
      <data key="d15">Keys are re-read once the TTL has elapsed.

    The clock is injected rather than slept through. An earlier version used
    ttl=0.0 and two back-to-back calls, which passes only if the monotonic
    clock ticks between them -- so it passed on one machine and failed on
    another, where Windows falls back to GetTickCount64's ~15.6ms granularity
    and both calls read the same instant.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">33</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="2042.50" y="2668.55" width="145.20" height="31.20" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_an_expire…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_auth.py::test_a_zero_ttl_never_caches">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_auth.py::test_a_zero_ttl_never_caches</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_a_zero_ttl_never_caches</data>
      <data key="d10">test_a_zero_ttl_never_caches</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_auth.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">585</data>
      <data key="d13">597</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_zero_ttl_never_caches():</data>
      <data key="d15">`ttl=0` means "do not cache", whatever the clock's resolution.

    With a strict `&gt;` comparison this promise silently depended on the clock
    ticking between calls, which is exactly the flake above in its other form:
    a configuration that says "never cache" would keep serving stale keys.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">32</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
