      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">71</data>
      <data key="d13">93</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss196_chunked_read_reports_the_same_digest_size_and_lines_as_a_whole_read(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">The digest and the line count used to come from a bytearray holding the
    entire file -- the one thing max_file_bytes exists to prevent. They are
    streamed now, and must still be the same numbers, both against the fixture
    bytes and against the whole-file reader on the same bytes.</data>
