    <node id="sym:tests/test_http_hardening.py::test_protocol_version_matches_what_this_transport_implements">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_http_hardening.py::test_protocol_version_matches_what_this_transport_implements</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_protocol_version_matches_what_this_transport_implements</data>
      <data key="d10">test_protocol_version_matches_what_this_transport_implements</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_http_hardening.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">98</data>
      <data key="d13">111</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_protocol_version_matches_what_this_transport_implements(make_server):</data>
      <data key="d15">#390: advertise the revision whose semantics are actually served.

    Pinned as a literal, not compared against the module constant the
    implementation itself uses -- `AGENTS.md`'s "never compare the
    implementation to itself" rule. This transport is plain JSON-RPC
    request/response over POST (Content-Length framing, HTTP/1.0,
    connection-close, no SSE, no Mcp-Session-Id): `2024-11-05` is the
    revision that describes, not `2025-06-18` (Streamable HTTP).</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6230.88" y="3419.45" width="130.07" height="27.95" />
