      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">117</data>
      <data key="d13">142</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_rsa_verify_weak_key_and_bad_signature_are_indistinguishable():</data>
      <data key="d15">#367: a caller must not be able to tell "weak key" from "bad signature".

    Both fail the *same* way inside `decode_jwt` -- a plain `AuthError("token
    signature is invalid")` -- because `rsa_verify` returns False for either
    rather than raising something distinct. Asserted directly against
    `rsa_verify`, matching the acceptance criteria in #367.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
