      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_http_hardening.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">854</data>
      <data key="d13">886</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_make_handler_binds_configuration_onto_the_handler_class():</data>
      <data key="d15">`BaseHTTPRequestHandler` is instantiated once per request, so everything
    a request needs has to live on the *class* -- `make_handler` is where that
    binding happens, and two fixes in this change depend on it being right:
    `self.repo` drives the auto-build tool annotations (#292), and
    `trust_proxy`/`trusted_proxies` decide whether `X-Forwarded-For` is ever
    consulted (#267). Both read attributes that nothing would notice were
    missing until a request arrived.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5701.38" y="3507.15" width="136.12" height="29.25" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
