      <data key="d14">def test_incremental_is_byte_identical_to_a_full_rebuild(tmp_path, mutate):</data>
      <data key="d15">The acceptance test: same bytes out, whatever route got there.

    Two checkouts of the same content, mutated identically. One is built fresh;
    the other is built once, mutated, then rebuilt incrementally. Every artifact
    must match byte for byte -- including `stats.json`, which is why the
    cached/re-parsed tallies live on `Graph.incremental` and not in `stats`.</data>
