    <node id="sym:tests/test_index_status.py::test_repo2graphs_own_scratch_files_do_not_mark_the_tree_dirty">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_index_status.py::test_repo2graphs_own_scratch_files_do_not_mark_the_tree_dirty</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_repo2graphs_own_scratch_files_do_not_mark_the_tree_dirty</data>
      <data key="d10">test_repo2graphs_own_scratch_files_do_not_mark_the_tree_dirty</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_index_status.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">372</data>
      <data key="d13">402</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_repo2graphs_own_scratch_files_do_not_mark_the_tree_dirty(built):</data>
      <data key="d15">A clean checkout must not record `dirty: true` because of repo2graph.

    `BuildLock` writes `..r2g.r2glock` and `dump_all` stages artifacts in
    `..r2g.staging.&lt;pid&gt;.&lt;hex&gt;/`, both *beside* the output directory so they
    survive the transactional swap -- which means `.r2g/` in .gitignore
    covers neither. Provenance is captured from inside both windows, so every
    build of a pristine repository used to report a dirty tree and blame the
    user for repo2graph's own scratch files.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="646.55" y="3824.80" width="142.18" height="30.55" />
