    <node id="sym:tests/test_output_schema.py::test_bundle_scrubs_paths_out_of_free_text_notes">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_output_schema.py::test_bundle_scrubs_paths_out_of_free_text_notes</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_bundle_scrubs_paths_out_of_free_text_notes</data>
      <data key="d10">test_bundle_scrubs_paths_out_of_free_text_notes</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_output_schema.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">711</data>
      <data key="d13">739</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_bundle_scrubs_paths_out_of_free_text_notes(indexed, monkeypatch):</data>
      <data key="d15">Prose assembled elsewhere must not be able to smuggle a path in.

    `compute_freshness` interpolates an exception message into a note, and an
    `OSError` carries the absolute path that failed -- so a discovery failure
    put an absolute path to `pkg/secret_roadmap.py` into a bundle that
    promises no absolute paths and no filenames. The happy path produces no
    such note, which is why the other privacy tests did not see it.

    Scrubbed at the boundary rather than in each producer: the guarantee has
    to hold for prose written by code that has never heard of the bundle.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
