    <node id="sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_a_diff_that_quotes_a_diff_does_not_rewrite_the_enclosing_file">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_a_diff_that_quotes_a_diff_does_not_rewrite_the_enclosing_file</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_a_diff_that_quotes_a_diff_does_not_rewrite_the_enclosing_file</data>
      <data key="d10">test_a_diff_that_quotes_a_diff_does_not_rewrite_the_enclosing_file</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_pr_impact.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">81</data>
      <data key="d13">134</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_diff_that_quotes_a_diff_does_not_rewrite_the_enclosing_file():</data>
      <data key="d15">Hunk *content* must never be read as a file header.

    Every line inside a hunk carries a `+`/`-`/space prefix, so a source line
    reading `++ b/oops.py` arrives as `+++ b/oops.py` and one reading
    `-- /dev/null` arrives as `--- /dev/null`. Matching those against the
    `+++ `/`--- ` header branches let a diff's own content rename the enclosing
    file, delete its entry, and flip its status -- so every symbol in the
    genuinely-changed file was skipped by `analyze_diff_impact`'s
    `path not in file_diffs` test and the report named a file never touched.
    A diff that merely quote</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5646.93" y="4340.55" width="133.10" height="28.60" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_a_diff_th…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_an_unparseable_file_header_does_not_bleed_into_the_previous_file">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_an_unparseable_file_header_does_not_bleed_into_the_previous_file</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_an_unparseable_file_header_does_not_bleed_into_the_previous_file</data>
      <data key="d10">test_an_unparseable_file_header_does_not_bleed_into_the_previous_file</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_pr_impact.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">137</data>
      <data key="d13">189</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_an_unparseable_file_header_does_not_bleed_into_the_previous_file():</data>
      <data key="d15">`diff --cc` and a git-quoted path both fail DIFF_GIT_RE -- and must still
    end the previous file's block.

    `current_hunk` used to be reset only on a successful DIFF_GIT_RE match, so a
    header this parser cannot split arrived with the *previous* file's hunk still
    open and its body lines were charged to that file. Phantom `added_lines` are
    load-bearing: `analyze_diff_impact` selects changed symbols from exactly that
    set, so the report names symbols the PR never touched.

    Combined diffs are not supported (`@@@` is not `HUNK_RE`), and that is fine --
    `get_git_diff` ne</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5804.03" y="4340.55" width="130.07" height="27.95" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_an_unpars…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_no_newline_at_end_of_file_does_not_advance_the_line_counter">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::test_no_newline_at_end_of_file_does_not_advance_the_line_counter</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_no_newline_at_end_of_file_does_not_advance_the_line_counter</data>
      <data key="d10">test_no_newline_at_end_of_file_does_not_advance_the_line_counter</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_pr_impact.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">192</data>
      <data key="d13">211</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_no_newline_at_end_of_file_does_not_advance_the_line_counter():</data>
      <data key="d15">`\\ No newline at end of file` is legal *mid*-hunk and is not a line.

    It follows the last line of whichever side lacks the trailing newline, so it
    can land between the `-` lines and the `+` lines. Counting it as a context
    line pushed every later `+` in the hunk down by one.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5958.10" y="4340.55" width="130.07" height="27.95" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_no_newlin…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
