    <node id="sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::flood_index">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_pr_impact.py::flood_index</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">flood_index</data>
      <data key="d10">flood_index</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_pr_impact.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1082</data>
      <data key="d13">1119</data>
      <data key="d14">def flood_index():</data>
      <data key="d15">An index wide enough that the tool's output ceiling actually binds.

    A bound asserted against a four-symbol fixture proves nothing (AGENTS.md's
    MCP rule says so explicitly), so this builds 300 files x 4 public symbols,
    each called from the next file, which is what makes the rendered report --
    symbols, callers, modules, dependency paths -- exceed the ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="4171.95" y="4429.55" width="106.95" height="29.90" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
