      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1401</data>
      <data key="d13">1423</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_impact_builds_a_missing_index_by_default(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">`--no-auto-build` only means something if building is the default.

    The flag was declared with `dest="auto_build"` but `args.auto_build` was
    never read, so `cmd_impact` always went straight to `_require_index` and a
    first run died with "no index at .r2g" — the documented default behaviour
    could not happen. Asserted through the report, not just an exit code: a
    build that produced no graph would still return 0.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5698.02" y="4429.55" width="142.18" height="30.55" />
