      <data key="d13">1742</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_the_backup_suffix_strip_terminates_on_a_hostile_name(path):</data>
      <data key="d15">A path is attacker-supplied on every build, and this rule loops.

    Each pass removes at least one character and the loop stops when no suffix
    matches or nothing but the suffix is left, so a name that is nothing but
    thousands of stacked suffixes must return rather than recurse without bound.
    The time bound is deliberately loose (measured ~6ms for the worst of these).</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
