    <node id="sym:tests/test_repo2graph.py::test_manifest_usage_hints_are_present_and_non_empty">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_repo2graph.py::test_manifest_usage_hints_are_present_and_non_empty</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_manifest_usage_hints_are_present_and_non_empty</data>
      <data key="d10">test_manifest_usage_hints_are_present_and_non_empty</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_repo2graph.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">713</data>
      <data key="d13">744</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_manifest_usage_hints_are_present_and_non_empty(tmp_path, sample_repo):</data>
      <data key="d15">usage_hints lets an agent orient without a round-trip tool call: every
    key is populated, and edge_type_meanings/what_is_not_indexed are derived
    from the same source manifest.json's top-level edge_types and the skip
    labels write_overview_human's "What was skipped" section uses -- not a
    second hand-authored copy that can drift.</data>
