      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">2533</data>
      <data key="d13">2581</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_parse_source_tsx_symbols_calls_and_imports():</data>
      <data key="d15">TSX LANG_CFG had zero direct parse_source coverage (kind_map extras / calls / imports).

    The snippet is JSX-bearing on purpose: LANG_CFG['tsx'] shares typescript's
    kind_map (interface / type alias / enum), but only the tsx grammar accepts
    JSX. A silent drift to the javascript map would drop those extras; pointing
    'tsx' at the non-JSX typescript grammar would ERROR the greet body and drop
    the function (parse_errors == 0 is the lock).</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
