    <node id="sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_node_and_edge_records_carry_their_documented_minimum">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_node_and_edge_records_carry_their_documented_minimum</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_node_and_edge_records_carry_their_documented_minimum</data>
      <data key="d10">test_node_and_edge_records_carry_their_documented_minimum</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_schema.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">43</data>
      <data key="d13">55</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_node_and_edge_records_carry_their_documented_minimum(mini_index):</data>
      <data key="d15">`export.FILE_NOTES` promises `id`/`type` on every node and
    `src`/`dst`/`type` on every edge -- NodeRecord/EdgeRecord are `total=False`
    (every field is type-specific), so this checks the one invariant that
    actually holds for all of them rather than a TypedDict's required set.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3527.18" y="5257.05" width="133.10" height="28.60" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_node_and_…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_every_emitted_node_and_edge_field_is_declared_in_schema">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_every_emitted_node_and_edge_field_is_declared_in_schema</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_every_emitted_node_and_edge_field_is_declared_in_schema</data>
      <data key="d10">test_every_emitted_node_and_edge_field_is_declared_in_schema</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_schema.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">58</data>
      <data key="d13">92</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_every_emitted_node_and_edge_field_is_declared_in_schema(mini_index):</data>
      <data key="d15">The direction the test above cannot see: a field emitted but undeclared.

    `NodeRecord`/`EdgeRecord` are `total=False`, so `__required_keys__` is the
    empty set and any "does the record carry what we declared" check is
    vacuously true for them. That left the *other* drift undetected, and it had
    accumulated: `start_line`, `end_line` and `signature` were emitted on every
    symbol node and declared nowhere -- the three keys `impact.py` reads -- along
    with `size`/`chunked`/`parse_errors`/`external` on nodes and the seven
    resolution/inheritance fields on edges.

    schema.py</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3684.28" y="5257.05" width="142.18" height="30.55" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_every_emi…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_inherits_and_external_records_are_declared">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_schema.py::test_inherits_and_external_records_are_declared</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_inherits_and_external_records_are_declared</data>
      <data key="d10">test_inherits_and_external_records_are_declared</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_schema.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">95</data>
      <data key="d13">155</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_inherits_and_external_records_are_declared(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">The edge and node types `mini_index` never produces.

    `mini_repo` has no class hierarchy and no call out of the tree, so the drift
    check above never sees an `INHERITS` edge (`raw_base`, `subtype`), a
    `CALLS_EXTERNAL` edge (`ambiguous`) or an `external` node -- 8 of the fields
    this module declares. A drift detector blind to a third of the surface is the
    kind of test that passes while the contract rots, so this builds a repo that
    does emit them rather than asserting against the same narrow fixture twice.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">207</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3850.45" y="5257.05" width="166.38" height="35.75" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_inherits_…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
