      <data key="d13">619</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_csharp_and_php_import_alias_fields():</data>
      <data key="d15">C# writes `alias = target`; PHP writes `target as alias`. Both were inverted.

    `using Foo = Bar.Baz;` parsed to `module='Foo', alias='Bar'`, so a call to
    `Bar(...)` resolved at confidence 1.0 to a symbol named `Foo` while the real
    alias resolved to nothing.</data>
