      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">712</data>
      <data key="d13">740</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_cache_without_resolution_evidence_is_refused(tmp_path: Path):</data>
      <data key="d15">A cache written before this PR must be rejected, not half-read.

    Its entries carry no `import_details`, `call_details` or `base_details`, so
    every cached symbol would come back with `call_kind='static'` and every
    aliased import unresolved. `PARSE_CACHE_FORMAT` is the only thing standing
    between such a cache and a silently wrong incremental build, which is why
    the constant has to move whenever an entry's shape does.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
