    <node id="sym:tests/test_secrets_hardening.py::test_repeated_begin_without_end_stays_linear">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_secrets_hardening.py::test_repeated_begin_without_end_stays_linear</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_repeated_begin_without_end_stays_linear</data>
      <data key="d10">test_repeated_begin_without_end_stays_linear</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_secrets_hardening.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">795</data>
      <data key="d13">812</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_repeated_begin_without_end_stays_linear():</data>
      <data key="d15">The detector for the quadratic form.

    At 200k characters the paired scan takes tens of milliseconds; the lazy
    single-pattern form took ~8 seconds, and ~8 minutes at the 1.5 MB file
    ceiling. The bound below sits far from both, so it survives a slow CI box
    without going vacuous.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5756.53" y="5404.50" width="133.10" height="28.60" />
